		{"id":"fa473298189117db","type":"group","x":10848,"y":-2784,"width":580,"height":1065,"label":"All three processes"},
		{"id":"cfb6f18dbf08378d","type":"group","x":10868,"y":-3980,"width":540,"height":1020,"label":"All three processes."},
		{"id":"4668ee5b78aaf5bb","type":"text","text":"# SP = 1. Metadata inference\n\n(Description, embedding_input, embedding_vector, foreign_keys)\n","x":10868,"y":-2764,"width":540,"height":264},
		{"id":"a74b3c5197cb4d67","type":"text","text":"# SP = 2. Relationship inference","x":10868,"y":-2404,"width":540,"height":264},
		{"id":"1bb592bc57672ae7","type":"text","text":"# SP = 3. Edge Metadata","x":10868,"y":-2040,"width":540,"height":260},
		{"id":"b71b310f89760b2b","type":"text","text":"1. Now there is small change in the small, when my api gets triggered i will search in the mongodb collection, by process_id which i have received from the payload.Below is the sample document\n    \n    ```json\n    {\n      \"process_id\": \"airbyte_sync-d4471983-b81f-1861-18-b81fd4471b94\",\n      \"source_id\": \"b8cac9b2-227b-4646-8416-3e7f55911d2d\",\n      \"table_id\": \"c6fbb5ca6219111731f9c4c4d2675810\",\n      \"column_id\": \"217338c042f487387a8ff4d671982140\",\n      \"event_type\": \"column_change\",\n      \"change_type\": \"insert\",\n      \"last_modified\": \"2025-09-03T14:58:34.412782\",\n      \"updated_by\": \"cdc\",\n      \"event_status\": \"N\"\n    }\n    ```\n    \n    By reading this i need to start the process.\n2. The framework should now is everytime is CIC, even if i am loading the data for the first time. Every time i am reading the data from the mongo collection as explained above and am i performing the task\n\nKey Development Answers:\n\n1. `change_source + insert`: Current `source_id` is sufficient ✓\n- `change_table + insert`: Need `source_id` + `table_id` (specific table being inserted)\n- `change_column + insert`: Need `source_id` + `table_id` + `column_id` (specific column being inserted)\n\nThis is correct but, what are the parameters do we need, we shouldn't send different parameters, we always send same parameters every time irrespective of the event_type and change_type.\n\n2. That is right, we need to infer only those tables which are being received, but the execution should be in the batch to reduce the timings(how i am doing currently)\n3. Yeah it does work by single column.\n4. Make changes in the robust way and it should be dynamic\n5. As i mentioned before, now there is no one time (there may be first time) it's always a CIC.\n\nNow i will below mention the High level code flow:\n\n**Code flow:**\n1. Get the process_id from the payload response\n2. search the process_id in the  delta log document \n3. Read the document\n4. Verify the event_status (should be not processed)\n5. Find the change_type\n6. Find the event_type\n7. **Run all the three sub processes**\n8. Update the result in the mongoDB\n9. Write the event_status to processes\n","x":4820,"y":-3091,"width":920,"height":820},
		{"id":"0963dafa88c78274","type":"text","text":"Hey. I am integrating the CDC (also we can call it as CIC-change inference capture) for my existing framework(which is one time). I need your help to integrate CIC in my framework.\n\nI will go on explaining the things what already exists and what needs to be done.\n\n**Current Flow:**\n1. I will receive multiple fields in payload but the main field in that payload is source_id. \n2. I have 3 sub process in my framework, **process 1** it does generates the description, embedding input for sources, rates the description, embedding input and foreign keys for tables, rates the description, embedding input for columns, in **process 2** i am generating the relationships in tables and in **process 3** i am creating the edges(links).\n3. source_id plays a vital role in my current framework where the code is completely depends on the source_id. what i mean is i am inferring to only those sources which i will receive in the payload. Lets say i receive the \"s_ga4\"  source, i only infer the s_ga4(related tables, columns)\n\n**Implementation Flow Pre-requisites:**\n1. I have made these for CIC integration.\n\t1. change_type: insert/update/delete\n\t2. event_type: change_source/change_table/change_column\n2. I have to read the documents of CIC then need to process my workflow.\n\n**Implementation Flow:**\n\n1. Now, the flow should change from inferring only received source to event_type and change_type.\n2. CIC should be implemented to all the three processes.\n\n**Note:**\n1. I will provide you the all the three processes one after one, analyse them\n2. Do not provide me the code until we clear with the design.\n3. I need the plan first how we are going to implement it.(may be in .md format)","x":3860,"y":-3140,"width":800,"height":1140},
		{"id":"3f0c0e54aa5c743f","type":"text","text":"**Change type - INSERT**\n\n| Event type | Parameters Required                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    | Blockers                                                                                                          | Comments                                                                                                                                                | Sub Process 1 - Embeddings                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         | Sub Process 2 - Relationships                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     | Sub Process 3 - Edges                                                                                |\n| ---------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| New Source | Source_id                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              | No blockers as of now.                                                                                            | Existing code base align with this functionality or logic                                                                                               | Current logic aligns with the flow.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                | Current logic aligns with the flow                                                                                                                                                                                                                                | Current logic align witht the flow                                                                   |\n| New table  | Source_id(helps us to infer in better way), table_id(vital component, in coming days it can be a list of new tables)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   | Foreign key(since it is not bidirectional update - if the client is giving out the foreign keys no issues here. ) | Need to overwrite the descriptions and necessary fields showcasing that we have accommodated the new table.                                             | Foreign key bidirectional check ( but for now lets park it.)                                                                                                                                                                                                                       | Yes we need to somehow pass the CDC documents. Pass the document id                                                                                                                                                                                               | Yes we need to somehow pass the CDC documents. Pass the documents id on which edge needs to created. |\n| New Column | Source_id ( not necessarily updating the source description since it might lead to narrowing down for this column only. ), table_id(tables description needs to be changed but very minimal changes needs to done it should be driven by the new column), column_id( need to accommodate the list of columns so that we can process it once, if not we can do the same multiple times) | With existing code block it is quite difficult to accommodate only column processing.                             | Need to build robust mechanism where it does the job based on the event type and change type ( we need to map the types somewhere with out tech logics) | It will generate the embedding, ( so we need to pass the column_id on which processing should be needed). How do you pass the column_id's only which processing should be done. <br>What if the incoming column is newly introduced primary key or foreign key of the other table. | It depends whether the new incoming column is PK or FK ? If they are not no procesing needed. If they are need to target the columns table ( anyways there is an bidirectional update which does the job, but need to pass only that column name for the process) | Need to think whether we run the complete task again by deleting the existing edges.                 |\n|            |                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        |                                                                                                                   |                                                                                                                                                         |                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    |                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |                                                                                                      |\n","x":20,"y":-3070,"width":1320,"height":1000},
		{"id":"ae77e520984c54d0","type":"text","text":"## Sub process 1 Table change Solution(FK)\n\nBusiness Aspect : \nNormally client will give out there foreign keys. If not anyways we have logic to pick it.\n\nTechnical Aspect :\nBlocker - If new table comes in and its primary key might be present as foreign keys in existing inferred tables, so at that moment we should be appending these values to the existing ones also as the FK. So we need \n\n\nFor now lets focus on the condition to take in the given foreign keys as continuing the process without we inferring the FK's. ( If FK field is null then we will do existing logic, if FK field is not null no process required.)","x":1620,"y":-2917,"width":756,"height":466},
		{"id":"35422adcc007313d","type":"text","text":"# Blockers \n\n1. In change_type insert and event_type is new source, if the source is sent in the list how will the tables are being sent. \n\t1. source_id: [\"123\", \"456\"] how we can bifurcate the tables. \n2. In change_type insert and event_type is new table, if the tables are sent in the list how will the columns are being sent.\n3. If there is new table to be inserted do i need to infer the source document again??\n4. If there is new table to be inserted do i need to re-infer the tables again (because of foreign keys?)","x":12228,"y":-3500,"width":680,"height":520},
		{"id":"fe609bc90e174843","type":"text","text":"# SP = 1. Metadata inference\n(Description, embedding_input, embedding_vector, foreign_keys)\n\n1. Get the source_id, table_id and column_id\n2. Infer the sources that are being received.\n3. Infer all the tables which are being received \n4. Infer all the tables which are being received","x":10888,"y":-3936,"width":500,"height":276},
		{"id":"f5cfe817249ffaf7","type":"text","text":"# SP = 2. Relationship inference\n(Relationship inference)\n\n1. Get the table_id and infer the relationship to only those tables.","x":10888,"y":-3600,"width":500,"height":260},
		{"id":"cd3a101fcb915268","type":"text","text":"# SP = 3. Edge Metadata\n(Creating Edges)\n\n1. Create the edges for only those received sources, tables, and columns.","x":10888,"y":-3236,"width":500,"height":256},
		{"id":"a4143e2e4600fbfb","type":"text","text":"# event_type is new_source\n\n1. Source_id: REQUIRED\n2. table_id: REQUIRED\n3. column_id: REQUIRED\n\n","x":9228,"y":-2580,"width":700,"height":220},
		{"id":"6df38b983bad1575","type":"text","text":"# event_type is new_table\n\n1. Source_id: REQUIRED\n2. table_id: REQUIRED\n3. column_id: REQUIRED","x":9228,"y":-2108,"width":700,"height":198},
		{"id":"28882250055fc0d9","type":"text","text":"Code flow:\n1. Get the process_id from the payload response\n2. search the process_id in the  delta log document \n3. Read the document\n4. Verify the event_status (should be not processed)\n5. Find the change_type\n6. Find the event_type\n7. **Run all the three sub processes**\n8. Update the result in the mongoDB\n9. Write the event_status to processes","x":8020,"y":-1571,"width":848,"height":411},
		{"id":"5fbc26f4be1887ee","type":"text","text":"# event_type is new_column","x":9270,"y":-1680,"width":617,"height":150},
		{"id":"c7f5d575f358a9dd","type":"text","text":"***change_type: insert***\n\n| Process       | new source                                                                                    | new table                                                                                                      | new column                                                                                                        | Blockers                                                                   |\n| ------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Sub Process 1 | Source inference, table inference, column inference for only given source_id.                 | Source inference, table inference, column inference for only given source_id and table_id.                     | No source inference, minimal table inference, column inference for only that received column.                     | What if the newly added column is foreign key or primary key of any table. |\n| Sub Process 2 | Relationship should be generated only for related source, related tables and related columns. | relationship should be inferred for only new added table. There may be a bi-directional updates it may happen. | Check whether it is a FK or PK if yes then there is a relationship for this column else no relationship inference | Finding out the FK or PK is the blocker.                                   |\n| Sub Process 3 | Process all the three steps, table to table, source to table, table to column                 | Process all the three steps, table to table, source to table, table to column                                  | Only table to columns process should be taken                                                                     | No blockers as of now.                                                     |\n\n\n","x":2373,"y":1677,"width":1180,"height":460,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"3f4cb0e3d6c02b94","type":"text","text":"Bronze Layer development plan:\n1. Add process called \"check CIC\" before ***metadata_inference*** process, When bronze layer API triggers check with the MongoDB *change_type* and *event_type*.\n\n***All the three process:***\n\n***1. insert_run_metadata_inference:***\n1. **For source_change:** No changes needed, all the processes like source inference, generating FK (if not present), generating description, generating embedding_inputs and generating embedding vectors remains same.\n2. **For table_change:** There should be source inference, generating FK, generating description, generating embedding_inputs and generating embedding vectors only for particular table(new table).\n3. **For column_change:** There should be no source inference, the inference must be only for newly added column. (need to think on what all data need to be passed to LLM for only column inference).\n\n***2. insert_run_relationship_inference:***\n1. **For source_change:** No changes needed, all the process like relationship inference for all the tables should happen like before.\n2. **For table_change:** Only relationship inference for given new table, there may be a chance of bi-directional updates.\n3. **For column_change:** If the column is FK or PK of any table then there should be relationship inference for that particular table, else skip the process.\n\n***3. insert_run_edge_metadata:*** \n1. **For source_change:** \n2. **For table_change:** \n3. **For column_change:**\n","x":-6960,"y":-3860,"width":1008,"height":1200,"color":"#2a0404"},
		{"id":"8debbc1510e7f8f8","type":"text","text":"| Event Type     | Parameters Required                                                                                                                                                                                                                  | Sub Process 1 - Embeddings                                                                                                         | Sub Process 2 - Relationships                                                                                                             | Sub Process 3 - Edges                                                                                           | Blockers                                                                                                                    | Comments                                                                                                                                                              |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **New Source** | `source_id`                                                                                                                                                                                                                          | Current embedding logic already aligns with this flow.                                                                             | Current relationship inference logic already aligns with this flow.                                                                       | Current edge logic already aligns with this flow.                                                               | No blockers as of now.                                                                                                      | Existing code base already supports this functionality.                                                                                                               |\n| **New Table**  | `source_id` (for better inference), `table_id` (mandatory). In future, may support multiple tables.                                                                                                                                  | Foreign key bidirectional check (deferred for now).                                                                                | CDC documents must be passed. Require `document_id`.                                                                                      | CDC documents must be passed. Require `document_id` for which edges need to be created.                         | Foreign key updates are not bidirectional by default. If the client provides foreign keys explicitly, this is not an issue. | Descriptions and required fields must be overwritten to reflect the new table.                                                                                        |\n| **New Column** | `source_id` (not always required for updating source description).`table_id` (minimal description changes driven by the new column).`column_id` (must support list of columns for batch processing; otherwise multiple runs needed). | Embedding will be generated. Must pass only the `column_id`s that require processing. Handle cases where new columns are PK or FK. | If not a PK/FK → no processing needed.If PK/FK → update bidirectional relationships, passing the column name to target the correct table. | Decide whether to re-run the full edge task (by deleting existing edges) or update only the affected column(s). | Current code block does not easily support column-only processing.                                                          | Need robust mechanism for column-level updates based on event type. Must support mapping without tight coupling. Special handling required if new column is PK or FK. |","x":-4545,"y":-3850,"width":1388,"height":689,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"87b1d58583e8e8f7","type":"text","text":"\n| Event Type        | Parameters Required | Sub Process 1 - Embeddings | Sub Process 2 - Relationships | Sub Process 3 - Edges | Blockers | Comments |\n| ----------------- | ------------------- | -------------------------- | ----------------------------- | --------------------- | -------- | -------- |\n| **Update Source** |                     |                            |                               |                       |          |          |\n| **Update table**  |                     |                            |                               |                       |          |          |\n| **Update Column** |                     |                            |                               |                       |          |          |\n","x":-4054,"y":-2970,"width":1388,"height":620,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"b0faa7eee4e4a5f4","type":"text","text":"**Code flow:**\n1. Get the process_id from the payload response\n2. search the process_id in the  delta log document \n3. Read the document\n4. Verify the event_status (should be not processed)\n5. Find the change_type\n6. Find the event_type\n7. **Run all the three sub processes**\n8. Update the result in the mongoDB\n9. Write the event_status to processes","x":-5580,"y":-2710,"width":600,"height":420,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"49c89567ecaafef8","type":"text","text":"| Event Type        | Parameters Required | Sub Process 1 - Embeddings | Sub Process 2 - Relationships | Sub Process 3 - Edges | Blockers | Comments |\n| ----------------- | ------------------- | -------------------------- | ----------------------------- | --------------------- | -------- | -------- |\n| **Delete Source** |                     |                            |                               |                       |          |          |\n| **Delete table**  |                     |                            |                               |                       |          |          |\n| **Delete column** |                     |                            |                               |                       |          |          |","x":-4226,"y":-2210,"width":1560,"height":600,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"557af1dcbdd2d625","type":"text","text":"1. If the change_type is insert and event_type is new_source assume it is a first time(may be the ingestion is 2/3rd time)\n2. `(source_id, table_id, column_id)` are the parameters that is being sent to all the processes.","x":13588,"y":-3340,"width":538,"height":200},
		{"id":"37cf8cc888c33e1a","type":"text","text":"1. If the change_type is insert and event_type is new_table infer only those tables which are inserted in the document.\n2. `(source_id, table_id, column_id)` are the parameters that is being sent to all the processes","x":13948,"y":-2932,"width":538,"height":194},
		{"id":"c8dc20f7ac9121ac","type":"text","text":"**1. \n\tchange_type: insert**\n\t**event_type: new_source**\n\n```json\n{\n\t\"process_id\": \"123\",\n\t\"source_id\": [\"qwerty\", \"1234\"],\n\t\"table_id\": \"\",\n\t\"column_id\": \"\",\n\t\"event_type\": \"new_source\",\n\t\"change_type\": \"insert\",\n\t\"event_status\": \"Not Processed\"\n}\n```\n\n**2.** \n\t**change_type: insert**\n\t**event_type: new_table**\n\n```json\n{\n\t\"process_id\": \"123\",\n\t\"source_id\": \"s1\",\n\t \"table_id\":  [\"t1\", \"t2\"],\n\t \"column_id\": \"\",\n\t \"event_type\": \"new_source\",\n\t\"change_type\": \"insert\",\n\t\"event_status\": \"Not Processed\"\n}\n```\n\n\n**3.**\n\t**change_type: insert**\n\t**event_type: new_column**\n```json\n{\n\t\"process_id\": \"123\",\n\t\"source_id\": \"s1\",\n\t\"table_id\": \"t1\",\n\t\"column_id\": [],\n\t\"event_type\": \"new_source\",\n\t\"change_type\": \"insert\",\n\t\"event_status\": \"Not Processed\"\n}\n```","x":12781,"y":-2596,"width":687,"height":880},
		{"id":"e547f5cb884e41c5","type":"text","text":"1. If the change_type is insert and event_type is new_column infer only those columns.\n2.  `(source_id, table_id, column_id)` are the parameters that is being sent to all the processes","x":14348,"y":-2543,"width":538,"height":215},
		{"id":"35f375dcec96a182","type":"text","text":"**Change type - INSERT**\n\n| Event type | Parameters Required                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    | Blockers                                                                                                          | Comments                                                                                                                                                | Sub Process 1 - Embeddings                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         | Sub Process 2 - Relationships                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     | Sub Process 3 - Edges                                                                                |\n| ---------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| New Source | Source_id                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              | No blockers as of now.                                                                                            | Existing code base align with this functionality or logic                                                                                               | Current logic aligns with the flow.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                | Current logic aligns with the flow                                                                                                                                                                                                                                | Current logic align witht the flow                                                                   |\n| New table  | Source_id(helps us to infer in better way), table_id(vital component, in coming days it can be a list of new tables)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   | Foreign key(since it is not bidirectional update - if the client is giving out the foreign keys no issues here. ) | Need to overwrite the descriptions and necessary fields showcasing that we have accommodated the new table.                                             | Foreign key bidirectional check ( but for now lets park it.)                                                                                                                                                                                                                       | Yes we need to somehow pass the CDC documents. Pass the document id                                                                                                                                                                                               | Yes we need to somehow pass the CDC documents. Pass the documents id on which edge needs to created. |\n| New Column | Source_id ( not necessarily updating the source description since it might lead to narrowing down for this column only. ), table_id(tables description needs to be changed but very minimal changes needs to done it should be driven by the new column), column_id( need to accommodate the list of columns so that we can process it once, if not we can do the same multiple times) | With existing code block it is quite difficult to accommodate only column processing.                             | Need to build robust mechanism where it does the job based on the event type and change type ( we need to map the types somewhere with out tech logics) | It will generate the embedding, ( so we need to pass the column_id on which processing should be needed). How do you pass the column_id's only which processing should be done. <br>What if the incoming column is newly introduced primary key or foreign key of the other table. | It depends whether the new incoming column is PK or FK ? If they are not no procesing needed. If they are need to target the columns table ( anyways there is an bidirectional update which does the job, but need to pass only that column name for the process) | Need to think whether we run the complete task again by deleting the existing edges.                 |\n|            |                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        |                                                                                                                   |                                                                                                                                                         |                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    |                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |                                                                                                      |\n","x":-7820,"y":-5740,"width":1320,"height":1000},
		{"id":"70250b06842b070d","type":"text","text":"***change_type: insert***\n\n| Process       | new source                                                                                    | new table                                                                                                      | new column                                                                                                        | Blockers                                                                   |\n| ------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Sub Process 1 | Source inference, table inference, column inference for only given source_id.                 | Source inference, table inference, column inference for only given source_id and table_id.                     | No source inference, minimal table inference, column inference for only that received column.                     | What if the newly added column is foreign key or primary key of any table. |\n| Sub Process 2 | Relationship should be generated only for related source, related tables and related columns. | relationship should be inferred for only new added table. There may be a bi-directional updates it may happen. | Check whether it is a FK or PK if yes then there is a relationship for this column else no relationship inference | Finding out the FK or PK is the blocker.                                   |\n| Sub Process 3 | Process all the three steps, table to table, source to table, table to column                 | Process all the three steps, table to table, source to table, table to column                                  | Only table to columns process should be taken                                                                     | No blockers as of now.                                                     |\n\n\n","x":-11040,"y":-2210,"width":1180,"height":460,"color":"5"}
